Resolves merge conflict when backporting negative value support in skew hints from main to branch-4.0.

## Conflict Resolution

The cherry-pick of commit 2dba160a introduced a merge conflict in `AstBuilder.java` where the new `visitGeneralLiteralExpression` method collided with the existing `visitIntegerValue` method signature.

**Changes:**
- Preserved new `visitGeneralLiteralExpression` method from main (handles negative literal values)
- Kept existing `visitIntegerValue` method signature from branch-4.0 (`StarRocksParser.IntegerValueContext` instead of `com.starrocks.sql.parser.StarRocksParser.IntegerValueContext`)
- Removed conflict markers

All other backport changes (grammar definitions, FloatLiteral constructor, tests) were already present in branch-4.0.

```java
@Override
public ParseNode visitGeneralLiteralExpression(
        com.starrocks.sql.parser.StarRocksParser.GeneralLiteralExpressionContext context) {
    if (context.literalExpression() != null) {
        return visit(context.literalExpression());
    } else {
        ParseNode node = visit(context.number());
        if (context.MINUS_SYMBOL() != null) {
            if (node instanceof IntLiteral) {
                return new IntLiteral(-((IntLiteral) node).getLongValue(), node.getPos());
            }
            // ... handles negative DecimalLiteral, FloatLiteral, LargeIntLiteral
        }
        return node;
    }
}

@Override
public ParseNode visitIntegerValue(StarRocksParser.IntegerValueContext context) {
    // Existing method preserved with branch-4.0 signature
}
```

